                projectiles_per_minute: 36
              assumed: []
    note: "Fire starts are theoretical: fires_per_minute = projectiles_per_minute x fire_chance, every projectile hitting a target that can burn. Not applied: the target's fire resistance and hull fire-node probability, the limit of fires burning at once, fire duration, dispersion and signal flags. Guns fire at their reload. A carrier squadron, which makes several attacks per sortie, attacks with attackerSize planes every attackCooldown, the shortest time between two of its attacks, while it has attacks left; flight to the target, returns and lost planes are left out, so this is its rate over the target. A squadron that attacks once per sortie, as hybrid ships launch them, attacks again when the hangar has restored its planes. An air strike releases every plane's ordnance once per consumable reload; its charges are not counted. Ordnance per attack is attackerSize x attackCount x projectilesPerAttack, the client's bombs per plane (PreprocessedPlanes). total adds the main battery's best ammo type, every secondary group, the best squadron of the stock plane modules (a carrier flies one at a time) and the best air strike aircraft (one air strike's aircraft share its charges)."
changes:
  - stat: Main Battery Reload Time
    from: 5.5 s
    to: 40.0 s
  - stat: Minimum Shell Type Switching Time
    from: 5.5 s
    to: 40.0 s
  - stat: Main battery damage per minute (HE)
    from: 366545 hp/min
    to: 140651 hp/min
  - stat: Main battery damage per minute (AP)
    from: 654545 hp/min
    to: 251163 hp/min
  - stat: "Fire starts per minute, all armament, every projectile hitting"
    from: 44.61 fires/min
    to: 28.80 fires/min
  - stat: "Main battery fire starts per minute, every shell hitting (HE)"
    from: 18.33 fires/min
    to: 2.52 fires/min
